lzug-admin - local administration for lzug

Usage:
  lzug-admin [global options] <object> <action> [options]
  lzug-admin [global options] cli

Objects:
  account            Manage operator accounts and one-time credentials.
  backup             Create, verify, and restore protected backups.
  committee          Bootstrap and maintain examination committees.
  completion         Generate shell completion scripts.
  config             Inspect local CLI configuration.
  export             Create and verify protected full exports.
  notification       Process and test technical notifications.
  plan-consequence   Inspect and retry confirmed-plan consequences.
  system             Inspect the local runtime and its readiness.
  upgrade            Apply upgrades and inspect rollback eligibility.
  cli                Start the guided interactive operator dialog.

Global options:
  --engine ENGINE          Container engine: auto, docker, or podman. Values: auto, docker, podman. Default: auto.
  --container NAME         Exact running container name.
  --config FILE            Read this explicit non-secret JSON configuration file.
  --no-config              Do not read a configuration file.
  --json                   Write exactly one machine-readable result object to stdout.
  --verbose                Write additional secret-free diagnostics to stderr.
  --force                  Skip an ordinary destructive-operation prompt.
  --help             Show global or contextual help.
  --version          Show the CLI version.
  --build-metadata   Show canonical build metadata as JSON.
